[I] An abstraction for enumerating power devices

[T] Upower is an abstraction for enumerating power devices,
[T] listening to device events and querying history and statistics.
[T] Any application or service on the system can access the
[T] org.freedesktop.DeviceKit.Power service via the system message bus.

[U] https://upower.freedesktop.org/

[A] David Zeuthen <davidz@redhat.com>
[M] Aldas Nabazas <baldzius@gmail.com>

[C] extra/development
[F] CROSS NO-LTO.clang

[E] opt gobject-introspection
[E] opt libimobiledevice libplist
[E] opt polkit

[L] GPL
[V] 1.91.5
[P] X -----5---9 142.500

[D] 66dc94f76f55677cd53fbad82d8291a1144d87cc75e5128e1ca9f60d upower-v1.91.5.tar.bz2 https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/upower/upower/-/archive/v1.91.5/

pkginstalled systemd || var_append mesonopt ' ' '-Dsystemdsystemunitdir=no -Dudevrulesdir=/etc/udev/rules.d/ -Dudevhwdbdir=/etc/udev/hwdb.d/'
pkginstalled gtk-doc docbook-xml docbook-xsl || var_append mesonopt ' ' -Dgtk-doc=false
pkginstalled libxslt docbook-xml docbook-xsl || var_append mesonopt ' ' -Dman=false
